Ladybird’s parse_shared_stylesheet() appends each top-level rule to the
sheet as soon as it’s consumed, and drops the rule’s component values
before it consumes the next one. Blink builds a sheet the same way:
CSSParserImpl::ParseStyleSheet() passes ConsumeRuleList() a callback
that appends each rule with ParserAppendRule(). So does WebKit, whose
CSSParser::parseStyleSheet() passes consumeRuleList() a callback that
calls parserAppendRule(). And Gecko’s Stylesheet::parse_rules() keeps
each rule as cssparser’s StyleSheetParser iterator yields it.
